# Topic access control.
#
# Participants share a broker, so without this every phone could subscribe to
# sensors/# and read every other participant's stream, or publish into their
# namespace. Access is keyed on the MQTT username, which is u<user_id>, and
# topics are namespaced to match.
#
# Regenerate the companion password file with scripts/sync_mqtt_users.sh
# whenever participants are added, then reload the broker.

# The backend ingests every participant's data and publishes status, so it is
# the only client with access to the whole tree.
user wearable_backend
topic readwrite #

# Each participant may publish only their own sensor data and read only their
# own status. %u expands to the connecting username, so one rule covers all of
# them and no participant can name another's namespace.
pattern write sensors/%u/#
pattern read status/%u/#
